          Revenue Code;

     -    satisfies the fiduciary standards of care established under ERISA;

     -    is subject to the unrelated business taxation rules under Section 511
          of the Internal Revenue Code; and

     -    constitutes a prohibited transaction under ERISA or the Internal
          Revenue Code.

     We intend to satisfy the "real estate operating company" exception to the
plan assets regulations promulgated pursuant to ERISA. Consequently, our assets
should not be treated as plan assets of an investing plan subject to ERISA. We
cannot assure you, however, that this exception will apply to our assets and, if
not, our assets may be treated as plan assets of an investing plan subject to
