exception for ownership of voting stock in a "qualified REIT subsidiary." A
qualified REIT subsidiary is a corporation that is wholly owned by a REIT
throughout the subsidiary's existence. For purposes of the asset and income
tests described below, all assets, liabilities and tax attributes of a qualified
REIT subsidiary are treated as owned by the REIT. A qualified REIT

